.TH ALDCONVERT 1 "2026-11-06" "AlphaDict 1.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
AldConvert \- convert AlphaDict XML files into an .aldict dictionary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B AldConvert
.B \-o
.I name
.I file.xml
.RI [ file.xml ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AldConvert
reads one or more XML files in the AlphaDict front-end format and writes a
single binary dictionary to
.IR name .aldict .
Several input files are merged into one dictionary, so a large word list can
be split into smaller files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-o " name"
Write the dictionary to
.IR name .aldict .
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a single XML file:
.PP
.RS 4
AldConvert \-o mydict words.xml
.RE
.PP
Merge several XML files into one dictionary:
.PP
.RS 4
AldConvert \-o mydict part1.xml part2.xml part3.xml
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR AlphaDict (1)
